   "system": {
    "source_reference": {
     "source": "fields_of_victory",
     "page": 91
    },
    "description": "<p>Many samurai wear a mempō, or mask, to cover their face on the battlefield. They use a mempō partially for both protection and intimidation. A mempō is crafted from iron or leather, covered with lacquer or clay, and painted to resemble a face. While some mempō may have human features, most showcase jagged oni teeth, a ferocious mouth, and a frightening expression. (Cost: 5 koku. Rarity: 4. Item Qualities: Ceremonial, Wargear.)</p>",
